        "nl-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "dcbf32cb-8df3-3907-ba4a-a535229f01b2",
                "word": "optooien",
                "pos": "verb",
                "lang_code": "nl",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2493a7bb-8f22-3e48-bf9c-614289d3e10c",
                        "entry_id": "dcbf32cb-8df3-3907-ba4a-a535229f01b2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "iets of iemand mooier maken"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "77251f2b-f2e3-4da3-8330-7d5a2c50abd7",
                                "sense_id": "2493a7bb-8f22-3e48-bf9c-614289d3e10c",
                                "text": "“Vrouwen hebben een veel langere traditie van zich mooi maken, optooien et cetera. Maar tegenwoordig moeten mannen ook goed ruiken."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5ce32720-c7e0-4d64-b8f5-31615022fdc6",
                                "sense_id": "2493a7bb-8f22-3e48-bf9c-614289d3e10c",
                                "text": "„Bij afwezigheid van de mannen, vonden pronkzieke vrouwen in overvloed van tijd en geld gelegenheid en tevens een aangename bezigheid in het oppronken van hun kamers en in het optooien van hun kledingstukken, naar eigen, en door omgang met anderen niet veranderde of beschaafde smaak; waarbij de ene de andere in kostbaarheid van stof en gekunstelde zorg zeker trachtte te overtreffen.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4ef33822-d70f-4b7c-a98b-311eea84418b",
                        "source_entry_id": "dcbf32cb-8df3-3907-ba4a-a535229f01b2",
                        "source_sense_id": "2493a7bb-8f22-3e48-bf9c-614289d3e10c",
                        "source_sense_description": "iets of iemand mooier maken",
                        "target_lang_word": "fit out",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "fit out",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cadcc8e3-9014-3713-afee-5368800a7f0b",
                                        "entry_id": "c2b07dcb-5d7a-3632-aeed-f8953750d8ea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To provide a thing, a group, a person or oneself with requisites; to kit out."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a4e7d01-2682-4a27-96c1-b76b519f209b",
                                                "sense_id": "cadcc8e3-9014-3713-afee-5368800a7f0b",
                                                "text": "On hearing of this determination, Mr. [John Jacob] Astor immediately proceeded to fit out a ship called the Enterprise, to sail in company with the Adams, freighted with additional supplies and reinforcements for Astoria."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "df668068-30f1-40f0-b6c9-697138957b6d",
                                                "sense_id": "cadcc8e3-9014-3713-afee-5368800a7f0b",
                                                "text": "On April 7, 1863, I received orders from General Rosecrans to proceed with the Provisional Brigade ... to Nashville, and to fit out as speedily as possible for an expedition to the interior of Alabama and Georgia, for the purpose of destroying the railroads and other rebel property in that country."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4a068216-4247-4818-8b75-dcc906488b22",
                                                "sense_id": "cadcc8e3-9014-3713-afee-5368800a7f0b",
                                                "text": "Moreover, if Bonaparte had wished to acquire territory in Australia, he was not so foolish a person as to fit out an expedition estimated to cost over half a million francs,^([2]) and which actually cost a far larger sum, when he could have obtained what he wanted simply by asking."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8f518d4d-6d27-4f34-a393-f5bc11dccb9c",
                        "source_entry_id": "dcbf32cb-8df3-3907-ba4a-a535229f01b2",
                        "source_sense_id": "2493a7bb-8f22-3e48-bf9c-614289d3e10c",
                        "source_sense_description": "iets of iemand mooier maken",
                        "target_lang_word": "furnish",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "furnish",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6a3c6e0c-c6cd-35f4-87c6-561fa01ef358",
                                        "entry_id": "771a9027-b563-3ebc-af36-361f5ae76e8b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Material used to create an engineered product."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1a1f6562-9476-4594-bb85-ce7a79642425",
                                                "sense_id": "6a3c6e0c-c6cd-35f4-87c6-561fa01ef358",
                                                "text": "The resin-coated furnish is evenly spread inside the form and another metal plate is placed on top."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "furnish",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "54b5699a-d6ef-37e0-9f05-87fb63ab0f47",
                                        "entry_id": "2c82533c-0291-36d9-935b-51495122e316",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To provide a place with furniture, or other equipment."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7cfa4d3c-e6ce-4a7e-8a5b-7515740486c0",
                                                "sense_id": "54b5699a-d6ef-37e0-9f05-87fb63ab0f47",
                                                "text": "The Celebrity, by arts unknown, induced Mrs. Judge Short and two other ladies to call at Mohair on a certain afternoon when Mr. Cooke was trying a trotter on the track. The three returned wondering and charmed with Mrs. Cooke; they were sure she had had no hand in the furnishing of that atrocious house."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5daec318-76cf-4e7b-9773-cbecbaa47213",
                                                "sense_id": "54b5699a-d6ef-37e0-9f05-87fb63ab0f47",
                                                "text": "Then his sallow face brightened, for the hall had been carefully furnished, and was very clean. ¶ There was a neat hat-and-umbrella stand, and the stranger's weary feet fell soft on a good, serviceable dark-red drugget, which matched in colour the flock-paper on the walls."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ba886f37-2846-362e-80be-5347f704e415",
                                        "entry_id": "2c82533c-0291-36d9-935b-51495122e316",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To supply or give (something)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "83e38f27-5365-43b3-9532-0952023f27a0",
                                                "sense_id": "ba886f37-2846-362e-80be-5347f704e415",
                                                "text": "[…] Miniſters are ſo wiſe to leave their Proceedings to be accounted for by Reaſoners at a Diſtance, who often mould them into Syſtems, that do not only go down very well in the Coffee-Houſe, but are Supplies for Pamphlets in the preſent Age, and may probably furniſh Materials for Memoirs and Hiſtories in the next."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3547b112-d3d5-4f4d-9627-3b7b99459539",
                                                "sense_id": "ba886f37-2846-362e-80be-5347f704e415",
                                                "text": "[H]e took his seat at the bottom of the table, by her ladyship's desire, and looked as if he felt that life could furnish nothing greater."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b310dfd1-1d74-4042-b0a7-4b9306170c6e",
                                                "sense_id": "ba886f37-2846-362e-80be-5347f704e415",
                                                "text": "But his writings and his life furnish abundant proofs that he was not a man of strong sense."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3296b9e1-8cff-36bd-84e7-42ae853285b4",
                                        "entry_id": "2c82533c-0291-36d9-935b-51495122e316",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To supply (somebody) with something."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74b6f763-2325-436e-9c51-b5f698a300ce",
                                                "sense_id": "3296b9e1-8cff-36bd-84e7-42ae853285b4",
                                                "text": "The street outside my window furnishes meager entertainment."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cfd66863-653d-4fa9-bb7a-becc2e87bc34",
                                                "sense_id": "3296b9e1-8cff-36bd-84e7-42ae853285b4",
                                                "text": "For, that the ordure, which continually gathers on the skin, would ſoon ſtop the pores of it, if the ſweat were not furniſht with ſome efficacious diſſolvent to open and pierce them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f190b4b3-2d16-48fb-b93d-d41626d5c5df",
                                                "sense_id": "3296b9e1-8cff-36bd-84e7-42ae853285b4",
                                                "text": "I was every day furniſhing the Court with ſome ridiculous Story; and Glumdalclitch, although ſhe loved me to Exceſs, yet was arch enough to inform the Queen, whenever I committed any Folly that ſhe thought would be diverting to her Majeſty."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e703ed26-8f4b-4e64-8c94-4767a16f67fe",
                                                "sense_id": "3296b9e1-8cff-36bd-84e7-42ae853285b4",
                                                "text": "[…] Mrs. Irons rebelled in her bed, and refused peremptorily to get up again, to furnish the musical topers with rum and lemons, […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
